Z||000000||DTH||12-30-2001||08:49 PM||||Just installed a rebuilt head. Hooked everything back up correctly to the best of my knowledge. Went to start it and it won't start it will fire but won't start. I'm getting spark to plugs. Getting fuel out of TBI. I noticed when trying to start that I get alot of fuel out of the TBI but when I floor the acc pedal the fuel stream stops but when I let off the stream comes back. Acts like its flooding itself. Haven't checked codes yet. Can you check codes without the engine running for some time? Hope this is enough info if not please ask for more.  THANKS  Dan ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Old Lar||12-30-2001||09:57 PM||||If the car hasn't been running since the head has been replaced, you won't get any current codes.  I'd guess the battery had been disconnected while you did the engine work, so you won't get any codes.  The car needs to run for 10-15 minutes while the ECM learns whats happening.<P>Recheck ignition wire loctions and connections.  Insure #1 cyliner is connected to #1 distributer position||||reg||1
